# Implementation Plan: Fix Branding Update & Asset Access

This plan addresses the "failed to update branding" issue by resolving storage accessibility problems and refining the frontend upload logic.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component Name] Backend Configuration

#### [EXECUTE] Run storage:link
- Establish the symbolic link between `storage/app/public` and `public/storage`. This is the primary reason why uploaded logos and signatures are appearing as broken images.

---

### [Component Name] Frontend Branding Logic

#### [MODIFY] [BrandingSettingsPage.tsx](file:///d:/learning/SkillPilot/skillpilot-frontend/src/app/%28dashboard%29/admin/settings/branding/page.tsx)
- Remove the manual `Content-Type: multipart/form-data` header from the `api.post` call. 
- **Reason**: Axios automatically handles the content-type and generates the necessary boundary delimiter when `FormData` is passed. Manually specifying it can lead to malformed requests on the server side.

---

### [Component Name] Backend Controller Logic

#### [MODIFY] [TenantBrandingController.php](file:///d:/learning/SkillPilot/skillpilot-backend/Modules/Tenants/app/Http/Controllers/TenantBrandingController.php)
- Enhance the validation for `brand_color` to support 3-digit hex codes (e.g., #000) for better flexibility, even though the current picker sends 6-digit codes.
- Add error logging to help debug if storage operations fail in certain environments.

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Create a new feature test `Modules/Tenants/tests/Feature/BrandingTest.php` to verify:
    - Successful update of color and files.
    - Retrieval of correct URLs.

### Manual Verification
- Use the browser subagent to:
    - Upload a sample logo.
    - Change the brand color.
    - Verify that images are no longer broken and changes persist.
